Kronos belonged to the [[Casterwill family]], and remained hidden in the Astronomical Clock of Prague for many years before being stolen by [[Viktor Casterwill]] in the seventeenth century. It was eventually passed down to his descendant, [[Dr. Benway]]. {{source|The Power of Kronos}}

Dr. Benway and [[the Professor]] fought each other for ownership of the Ring of Kronos with the Professor coming out victorious. He used [[Araknos]] to put Benway in a wheelchair for good and become a loyal scientist and advisor to him. The Professor often attempted to summon Kronos but never succeeded. {{Source|The Power of Kronos}}

After the defeat of the Professor, Dr. Benway reclaimed Kronos's Ring, and also helped himself to the most powerful Titans in the Organization's collection. {{source|The Power of Kronos}} When the Huntik team attempted to obtain the Ring, Benway set a trap and lured them to his base. Summoning Kronos, he attempted to use Kronos to wipe [[Lok]] and [[Sophie]] from existence, but missing, created a vortex that sucked in, sending them back in time to the seventeenth century. 

There, they found the Ring in the Astronomical Clock but were interrupted by Viktor Casterwill and [[Michel de Notre Dame]]. After defeating Viktor, Lok and Sophie found they had changed history by stopping the Ring falling into the hands of his lineag, thus preventing it from ever falling into the hands of Dr. Benway. After explaining the situation to Michel, he agreed to use Kronos and help them get home. The Casterwill Council then hid the Amulet of Kronos elsewhere. In the modern day, it was seen to be in a clock workshop as the ring on the shop employee's hand. {{Source|The Power of Kronos}}
